laurent|FIFA — Lucien Laurent, the first World Cup goalscorer|https://inside.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/1930uruguay/news/lucien-laurent-the-first-world-cup-goalscorer|France's Lucien Laurent scored the first World Cup goal against Mexico on 13 July 1930 in Montevideo; France won 4-1; Ernest Liberati supplied the cross. Verified 2026-10-07.
pickles|FIFA — Pickles and the stolen World Cup|https://inside.fifa.com/en/news/pickles-and-the-stolen-world-cup-2771152|The trophy was stolen in London on 20 March 1966 from a stamp exhibition at Methodist Central Hall, Westminster. Pickles and owner David Corbett recovered it wrapped in newspaper one week later. Verified 2026-10-07.
pozzo|FIFA — Pozzo prepares Azzurri push|https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/1934italy/news/pozzo-prepares-azzurri-push-2769391|Vittorio Pozzo coached Italy to the 1934 and 1938 World Cup titles. Verified 2026-10-07.
italy38|FIFA — Double joy for Pozzo's Italy|https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/1938france/news/double-joy-for-pozzo-s-italy|Italy defeated Hungary 4-2 in the 1938 final, with Gino Colaussi and Silvio Piola scoring two goals each. France hosted the tournament. Verified 2026-10-07.
maracanazo|FIFA — Uruguay's stunning upset of Brazil|https://www.fifa.com/en/articles/uruguay-brazil-1950-maracanazo|Uruguay beat Brazil 2-1 at the Maracana on 16 July 1950. Juan Alberto Schiaffino and Alcides Ghiggia scored Uruguay's goals; Brazil needed only a draw. Verified 2026-10-07.
