final70|FIFA — Brazil v Italy, Mexico 1970 final|https://www.fifa.com/pt/tournaments/mens/worldcup/articles/brasil-italia-final-copa-mundo-1970|Brazil beat Italy 4-1 at Estadio Azteca. Brazil's scorers were Pele, Gerson, Jairzinho and Carlos Alberto; Roberto Boninsegna scored for Italy. Brazil earned permanent possession of the Jules Rimet Trophy. Verified 2026-10-07.
final74|FIFA — Neeskens just about holds his nerve|https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/1974germany/news/neeskens-just-about-holds-his-nerve-2840562|Johan Neeskens opened the final with a penalty; Paul Breitner equalised with a penalty; Gerd Muller scored the winner before half-time. Helmut Schon coached West Germany. Verified 2026-10-07.
