balls|FIFA — The adidas Telstar begins ball chain|https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/1970mexico/news/telstar-story-fifa-world-cup-ball-3073424|Telstar debuted in 1970 with 32 leather panels for visibility on black-and-white television. Tango 1978; Azteca 1986; Etrusco Unico 1990; Questra 1994; Tricolore 1998 first coloured ball; Fevernova 2002; Teamgeist 2006; Jabulani 2010 eight panels; Brazuca 2014 six panels; Telstar18 embedded NFC chip. Verified 2026-10-07.
cards|FIFA — Gripping tales and inspirational traffic lights|https://inside.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/1966england/news/1966-world-cup-gripping-tales-and-inspirational-traffic-lights-2812820|Ken Aston devised yellow and red cards after 1966, inspired by traffic lights. They debuted in 1970. Rudolf Kreitlein dismissed Argentina captain Antonio Rattin in 1966. Aston refereed the Chile-Italy Battle of Santiago in 1962. Verified 2026-10-07.
fastgoals|FIFA — Fastest goals in World Cup history|https://www.fifa.com/en/articles/quickest-fastest-goals|Hakan Sukur scored at eleven seconds against Korea Republic in 2002; Vaclav Masek at fifteen seconds in 1962; Bryan Robson at twenty-eight seconds in 1982; Clint Dempsey at thirty seconds in 2014. Verified 2026-10-07.
